# Project conventions

Invariants, files not edited by hand and the status markers are in `ai/AGENTS.md`; this file adds the detail.

## Stack

Vite 7, React 18, TypeScript strict, react-router 7, Redux Toolkit + RTK Query, zod, SCSS Modules, Vitest 4 + Testing Library + msw.

Not in the project — don't add: MUI, styled-components, emotion, react-query, axios, yup, react-hook-form, i18next.

## Layout

- FSD layers under `src/`, high to low: `app` → `pages` → `widgets` → `features` → `entities` → `shared`.
- `src/utils/` sits outside the layers and holds mostly the PlayCanvas wrappers (`src/utils/functions/playcanvas/`); treat it like `shared`.
- `@/` is the alias for `src/`. Use relative imports inside a slice.
- Entry: `src/main.tsx` → `src/app/App.tsx` → `src/app/router/AppRouter.tsx` → `src/app/router/routerConfig.tsx`.

## Imports between slices

- **[needs decision]** A slice's `index.ts` as its only public API. Many production files import internals of slices that have one (e.g. `@/entities/configuration/model/store/selectors`). When the index already exports what you need, import from it; don't add exports to it or rewrite existing deep imports as a side task.
- Slices without an `index.ts` (e.g. `entities/product`, `entities/history`, `features/configurator-rule-core`, `features/sidebar`, `features/quotePrint`) are imported by file path. Don't add an index as a side task.
- **[needs decision]** Layer-root barrels exist — `src/{entities,features,pages,shared,widgets}/index.ts`, all `export *`. `@/shared` is used widely, the others by the router and a few files. Don't add exports to them as a side task.
- `src/entities/collection/index.ts`: the sections owned by C, I and B list re-exports by name, so a name collision fails to compile (rationale in the comment above the C section); the A section at the top uses `export *`. Add new C, I and B exports by name.
- Tests may import internals and fixtures of any slice.

## Layer direction

- **[needs decision]** Lower layers don't import higher ones. Current code breaks this in many places: `shared` → `entities` / `features` (pricing, SKU, hooks, popups), `entities` → `features` (including `src/entities/collection/lib/loadCollection.ts` and `src/entities/product/model/store/slice.ts`), `utils` → `entities`. These are legacy, not a template.
- Allowed from any layer: `import type { RootState, AppDispatch } from "@/app/store"`.
- The `store` value belongs to `src/app/` and tests. A few production files import it (e.g. `src/features/bottomCanvasButtons/BottomCanvasButtons.tsx`); don't copy that — components get the store through `useStore` / `useAppDispatch`, as `src/features/configurationCommands/hooks/useChangeAttribute.ts` does.

## State

- One RTK store: `src/app/store/index.ts`. UI slices live under `rootStateUI` (`src/app/store/reducer.ts`), including `features/sidebar` and `features/swatchOrder`; RTK Query lives under `api`.
- **[observed]** Components use `useAppSelector` / `useAppDispatch` from `src/shared/hooks/store/redux.ts`; production code has no raw `useSelector` / `useDispatch`.
- Cross-slice reactions live in the listener middleware `src/app/store/optionsListener.ts`, which also registers listeners from features (`setupSceneStateListener`, `setupSidePanelListener`). Listener typing: `ai/typescript_typing_contracts.mdc` rule 6.
- Examples: `src/entities/configuration/model/store/slice.ts`, `src/entities/history/model/store/slice.ts`.

## Backend API

- Each entity injects its endpoints into `baseApi` (`src/shared/api/baseApi.ts`) from `src/entities/<slice>/api/`: `<slice>Api.ts`, `routes.ts`, `types.ts`, `index.ts`.
- Response types are hand-written. Check them against real responses or the frozen fixtures; never guess.
- Example: `src/entities/countertop/api/countertopApi.ts` with its msw test `src/entities/countertop/api/__tests__/countertopApi.test.ts`.

## Collection data

A collection is a folder `public/collections/<id>/` (manifest, product-profile, ui, presets and, depending on the collection, sku-profile, runtime-bindings…) listed in `public/collections/registry.json`. Every collection has a `runtime-bindings.json`. A `state-only` value counts as applied without a scene call; an `unbound` attribute returns `unsupported` (`createPlayCanvasRuntimePort.ts`).

- `src/entities/collection/lib/loadCollection.ts` loads and validates a collection once; `CollectionReadinessGate` (`src/entities/collection/ui/CollectionReadinessGate.tsx`) opens the app only for a ready collection.
- Components read the data with `useActiveCollection(selector)` (`src/entities/collection/ui/activeCollectionContext.ts`) or a derived hook such as `useCountertopRules()` (`src/features/configurator-rule-core/countertop/hooks/useCountertopRules.ts`).
- One validator per file; don't add a second one (rationale: the comment on `productProfile` in `src/entities/collection/model/schemas.ts`):
  - registry, manifest → zod schemas in `src/entities/collection/model/schemas.ts`;
  - product profile → `parseProductProfile`;
  - runtime bindings → `parseRuntimeBindings`;
  - ui → `validateCustomizationSchema`.
- Reason codes: rules, commands and pages return `"namespace.camelCase"` codes (pages keep them as `REASON_*` constants). The text comes from the profile's `messages`, never from code. **[enforced]** for the USH profile only; `class` and `mako` declare no `messages` — **[needs decision]** whether every collection must.
- Background: `docs/collection-data-migration-status-v4.md`, `docs/product-profile-migration.md`.

## Scene

- Change path: UI → `useChangeAttribute` / `useChangeDimension` (`@/features/configurationCommands`) → change plan → `ConfigurationRuntimePort` (`src/entities/configuration/model/runtimePort.ts`, types only) → `src/features/playCanvasAdapter/lib/createPlayCanvasRuntimePort.ts` → `src/utils/functions/playcanvas/sceneBridge.ts`. The store is written by `src/features/configurationCommands/lib/commitChange.ts`.
- Dividers have their own scene adapter: `src/features/dividers/adapter/`.
- In `src/entities/collection/__tests__/collectionConsumerBoundary.test.ts`: allowed places for direct scene calls — `SCENE_INFRASTRUCTURE`; the calls — `directSceneCalls`; files still waiting, with owner and reason — `PENDING_DIRECT_SCENE_CALLERS`, `PENDING_DIRECT_STATE_WRITERS`, `PENDING_LEGACY_ALIAS_CALLERS`, `PENDING_PAGE_CATALOGS`.
- Scene keys and values come from the collection's `runtime-bindings.json`.
- Debugging in the browser:
  - `window.__configuratorApiLogs` — scene API call log (`src/utils/functions/playcanvas/apiLogger.ts`);
  - `window.__HASTING_DIVIDER_UI_DEBUG__.dump()` — divider UI state (`src/utils/functions/playcanvas/dividers/dividerUiDebug.ts`).
- Background: `docs/runtime-bindings-migration.md`.

## Tests

- Vitest runs only `src/**/__tests__/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}` (`vitest.config.ts`). The default environment is `node`; DOM tests start with `// @vitest-environment jsdom`.
- Integration tests use the real `store` and reset its slices in `beforeEach` (e.g. `src/entities/collection/__tests__/fixtureUiStateIntegration.test.tsx`).
- Helpers:
  - synthetic collection — `renderWithFixtureCollection` (`src/entities/collection/__tests__/fixtures/renderWithFixtureCollection.tsx`); the fixtures are described in `fixtures/README.md` there;
  - shipped USH data — `ushProfile` (`src/entities/collection/__tests__/ushProfileFixture.ts`) and `ushRuntimeBindings` (`src/entities/collection/lib/runtimeBindings/__tests__/ushRuntimeBindingsFixture.ts`);
  - backend API — msw;
  - scene — `createTestRuntimePort`, `createTestSceneReader`, `createTestSceneRestorer` from `@/features/playCanvasAdapter`.
- Source-scanning checks read `src` through `import.meta.glob(..., { query: "?raw" })`; see `collectionConsumerBoundary.test.ts` and `reasonCodesHaveMessages.test.ts`. A waiting list carries an owner, a reason and an exact count.
- `src/shared/lib/pricing/__tests__/recordPriceFixtures.test.ts` is skipped unless `RECORD_PRICES=1` and is excluded from `tsc`.

## Ownership

Code comments and tests name owners (e.g. the section comments in `src/entities/collection/index.ts`, the `Residue` type in `collectionConsumerBoundary.test.ts`):

- A — collection loading;
- B — pages and the UI schema;
- C — product profile, state and commands;
- D — pricing;
- I — scene and runtime bindings.

Keep the owner comments when editing those sections. Some comments cite "CONTRACTS §N"; that document is not in the repository.
